{"title":"Partition of an interval","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>partition of an interval</b> is a division of an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Interval\" title=\"Interval\">interval</a> into several disjoint sub-intervals.  Partitions of intervals arise in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Calculus\" title=\"Calculus\">calculus</a> in the context of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral#Riemann_Integral\" title=\"Integral\">Riemann integrals</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Norm\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Norm</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Tags\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Tags</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition\">Definition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition_of_an_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecbd1ba3da8f2adef66a63f2ab32c47e63fa734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[a,b]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> be an interval of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a>.\n</p><p>A <b>partition</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is defined as the ordered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tuple\" title=\"Tuple\">tuple</a> of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/0/8c00209bf77224a60f916b725141a05ac2313c56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}=(x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"154\" height=\"18\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/7/9a7c9a8316ffb3d433f2bf7cc306d4994e20c932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=x_0&lt;x_1&lt;\\ldots&lt;x_n=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"215\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Norm\">Norm</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition_of_an_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Norm\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The <b>norm</b> of a partition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c4598798275a046d30fc332b75b62f544b149e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\|\\mathcal{P}\\|=\\sup\\{x_i-x_{i-1}\\}_{i=1}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"193\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Tags\">Tags</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition_of_an_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Tags\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/6/9465ce8f688397601d7968a018d542148e2db821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" /> be a partition.\n</p><p>A <b>Tagged partition</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/e/d7e0599a6618d30957619f214699749da9938ad7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{\\dot{P}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is defined as the set of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4a621081b8c5c6b18dfd7163da5adfe7dcb1a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{\\dot{P}}=\\{([x_{i-1},x_i],t_i)\\}_{i=1}^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"178\" height=\"21\" />. \n</p><p>Where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5ccc7a9f346fe87c367fc7805876bab3cf139528.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i-1}&lt;t_i&lt;x_i\\forall t_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" />. The points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/3/273e0046b505d99f3d1167caa82b2ac76c96d075.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are called the <b>Tags</b>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Partition_of_an_interval&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral\" title=\"Integral\">Integral</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Riemann_sum\" title=\"Riemann sum\">Riemann sum</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Gauge\" title=\"Gauge\">Gauge</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Partition_of_an_interval&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018081714\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 83/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2315/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.534      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.534      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6436:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018081714 and revision id 172408. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}